ough Tucson's street curbs to steal stormwater]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132685573.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1998-an-arizona-man-secretly-cut-holes-through-tucsons-street-curbs-to-steal-stormwater-the-illegal-experiment-eventually-changed-city-policy/articleshow/132685573.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1998-an-arizona-man-secretly-cut-holes-through-tucsons-street-curbs-to-steal-stormwater-the-illegal-experiment-eventually-changed-city-policy/articleshow/132685573.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-28T20:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132685573,imgsize-3096450.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rescued After 30 Days Adrift: Solo sailor Kai Sato survives on scraps; container ship pulls him to safety]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132686957.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A California man survived thirty days adrift at sea after his sailboat lost its mast. Kai Sato was found nearly nine hundred miles from Hawaii by a container ship crew. He improvised repairs and collected condensation for water while surviving on limited food. The rescue operation took about an hour and a half to complete successfully. Sato expressed deep gratitude to the ship's crew for saving his life.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/he-ran-out-of-water-but-not-luck-california-mans-mast-broke-and-phone-died-after-30-days-alone-in-the-pacific-a-container-ship-found-him-900-miles-from-hawaii/articleshow/132686957.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatime